Good storage and distribution practices for medical products — WHO (@cs-who-storage: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_64EPQ96J7NE7QCWQ28SPXJ8V4D
World Health Organization. Good storage and distribution practices for medical products, TRS 1025, Annex 7, 2020. [Publication and full download](https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/trs-1025-annex-7/).

Read the whole annex, including quality, storage, stock rotation, equipment, qualification, transport, contracted activity and documentation. Compare its medical-product scope with the starting-material annex instead of assuming a single guideline covers all chemical trade. The quality/state history exercises use it as a detailed institutional example.

The official record dates publication 17 June 2020 and lists 20 pages; its currently linked PDF contains 32 file pages. Preserve that distinction and the title/page numbering actually read. The record and download were checked on 29 October 2026; not every external reference was inspected. Reuse follows the WHO publication and component notices. No medical-product or chemical-handling certification is implied and no file is bundled.

